<https://miraeasset.com/ontology/financial-product> a owl:Ontology ;
    rdfs:label "Mirae Asset Financial Product QA Ontology"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """
Implementation rule:
- Do not materialize PriceObservation, NAVObservation, PerformanceObservation,
  YieldObservation, FeeObservation, or other high-churn metric nodes in RDF for
  the competition QA runtime.
- Store numeric and time-varying values in RDB keyed by canonical product,
  fund-share-class, bond, or sale-lot identifiers.
- Store stable product, organization, identifier, index, classification,
  channel, and grain relations in the graph.
- Keep long-form overseas ETP strategy text in Vector/BM25.
- Preserve source dataset, row, column, and raw value metadata so the
  Answerability Gate can validate every factual claim before generation.
"""@en,
        """
Merged ontology for the Mirae Asset Agent AI competition.
This ontology uses the snapshot v7 design as the semantic and runtime backbone:
stable product, organization, identifier, index, classification, fund share-class,
and bond sale-lot relations are stored in the graph, while numeric and
time-varying metrics remain RDB-backed.

The stronger parts of the modular ontology are retained as validation and
provenance layers: source datasets, source records, source field assertions,
same-product candidates, strict identifier validation, ISIN format checks, and
identifier collision detection.
"""@en ;
    owl:versionInfo "merged-optical-1.4" .

